# Club & Grub - World 5, stage 1 in co-op: "Red Mesa Trail" (designer D5). The co-op file of levels/w5_l1.lvl
# (DESIGN.md D.10, LEVEL_DESIGN.md 15.7): the same map with P2's start, a pair of spears at the first checkpoint, signs
# for the egg and the x2 tablet, and three co-op gates on the main path, each with its tablet and a checkpoint behind:
#  - 'hop': the mesa steps of the solo file are one cliff 8 rows over a flat floor on both difficulties (a lone
#    player's idle partner is a 98 px Totem step, and its feet in a 7-row ledge's top cell catch the corner); one hero
#    stands under it, the other Shoulder-Hops off his head (140 px), then strikes the rolled vine at the edge - it
#    unrolls down to the floor, the way up for the partner (the coil is out of every throw from the floor);
#  - 'plates': a leapfrog plate door - the mesa's lower tunnel opens while plate A is held, its upper tunnel while
#    plate B beyond the mesa is held (each plate 8+ tiles from its door);
#  - 'gully': two Shellbacks keep the gully under the plain (a hall exactly 4 rows high); one hero baits the shield
#    while the other, dropped in through a hole behind it, clubs its back; the keeper door opens when both are dead.
# The Rollers of the long climb carry `shell` (G36: as one bond 'climb' a single thrown special could hit two
# members; the lead designer's ruling, applied by integration in phase 3 - the routes jump them unchanged); the first
# Roller, the plateau Roller and tortoise, the Expert Roller of the plain and the Expert eagle are left out (a bounce
# for a lone hero at the hop cliff, or a hit on a plate holder or a baiter).

[meta]
format = 2
id = w5_l1_coop
name = "Red Mesa Trail"
kind = coop
